>>>markdown
# Questionable Football: who to draft in 2026, and why

A walk from last season's scoring to next season's draft board, in the order a fantasy manager would ask the questions. Every number comes from a query below, so the notebook stays true when the data is rebuilt; the prose only says what each step is asking. Scoring is half-PPR over weeks 1-17, worked out from the play-by-play rather than taken from a provider.

>>>malloy
import "fantasy.malloy"
import "market.malloy"

>>>markdown
## Who scored in 2025?

The 2025 leaderboard, top 25. Each row is one player-season: total points, points per game, where the points came from, and the finish overall and at the position.

>>>malloy
run: player_seasons -> leaderboard + { where: season = 2025; limit: 25 }

>>>markdown
## Where do the points come from at each position?

Passing, rushing, receiving and kicking points by position across all three seasons, with the share that came from touchdowns. The touchdown share is the most volatile part of a season, so a position that leans on it is harder to project.

>>>malloy
run: fantasy_events -> scoring_mix

>>>markdown
## How steep is the drop at each position?

The average season of a top-6 finisher, a 7th-12th and a 13th-24th, over 2023-2025. A steep drop means waiting costs more; a flat one means the position can wait. This is the query behind the saved finding *The tight end cliff*.

>>>malloy
run: player_seasons -> position_cliff

>>>markdown
## Did the 2025 draft market price players well?

Each 2025 pick against where the player finished at their position. A hit is a finish at or above the drafted position rank; a player who never scored is a miss. The early rounds are where the misses were most expensive. This is the query behind the saved finding *Late picks beat their price*.

>>>malloy
run: adp_2025 -> hit_rate_by_phase

>>>markdown
The same picks by position and phase, to see which positions the early-round misses came from.

>>>malloy
run: adp_2025 -> hit_rate_by_round

>>>markdown
The largest misses of 2025: picks that finished furthest below their price.

>>>malloy
run: adp_2025 -> biggest_misses

>>>markdown
## Who does the 2026 market undervalue?

Players whose projected rank at their position is better than the rank the market drafts them at, with value over replacement: projected points above the last starter at the position in a 12-team league (QB12, RB30, WR36, TE12).

>>>malloy
run: draft_board -> market_steals

>>>markdown
And the other side: players the market drafts ahead of their projection.

>>>malloy
run: draft_board -> overpriced

>>>markdown
## Which teams does Vegas like?

The 2026 futures board: win totals, the wins implied by the posted game lines, and the 2025 record they are measured against. A team whose line-implied wins sit well above its win total is one the weekly markets like more than the season market does.

>>>malloy
run: team_outlook -> league_board

>>>markdown
## Which 2026 games should score the most?

The posted games with the highest over/under, where the players on both sides have the most room to score.

>>>malloy
run: schedule_2026 -> shootouts
